# Root .dockerignore — applies to the `web` image's build context (repo
# root; see apps/web/Dockerfile's header comment for why the context is the
# root and not apps/web). Does NOT affect the `api` image, which builds from
# its own ./apps/api context and has its own .dockerignore there.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.next
apps/web/.next

# Machine-local env files must NEVER enter a build context: `next build`
# loads .env.local (production included), so a dev machine's local values
# would be baked into the image. .env.example is documentation, not needed
# at build.
.env*
**/.env*

# apps/api is a separate build context (its own Dockerfile + .dockerignore);
# excluding it here just keeps the `web` build's context transfer small.
apps/api

# apps/web/demo is the `npm run demo` stub backend + its fixtures (~330MB,
# mostly captured preview HTML/assets) — unused by `next build`/`next
# start` (nothing under app/, components/, lib/, or hooks/ imports from it;
# verified by grep at batch-07 Task 4). Excluding it is most of this file's
# actual context-size win.
apps/web/demo

docs
logs
.specstory
.superpowers
.claude
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
